A9. An expert side-stepper. ~ CRAB
A13. This is a perfect howl. ~ RAVE
A14. You do this to locate that certain party. ~ PAGE
A15. What runners do in college. ~ RACE
A16. A good place for your dough. ~ OVEN
A17. A very small piece of Einstein material. ~ ATOM
A18. What Methuselah did in order to grow so old. ~ AGED
A19. The best of friends have done this. ~ PARTED
A21. Beach gods. ~ SAVERS
A23. This is entirely out of place. ~ INEPT
A26. A personal pronoun. ~ ME
A27. This will wreck your home life. ~ BLAST
A30. An astronomer better look into this. ~ AIR
A32. What a "bear" always lies in wait for. ~ DROP
A36. This will be over your head if you come in late through the window. ~ LINTEL
A38. Here's what the song-writer thought of Mary. ~ PAL
A40. Hail. ~ AVE
A41. A busy worker at a lawn party. ~ ANT
A42. Get-up. ~ RIG
A44. What Miss Lenglen is famous for. ~ TEMPER
A46. Another reason why the professor worked out his theory in Germany. ~ BEER
A48. It's too bad to feed this and then lose it. ~ POT
A50. A poetical yard-stick. ~ METRE
A51. The Glynn pronoun. ~ IT
A53. A German high-hat. ~ BARON
A55. Putting your cards on the table. ~ CANDOR
A59. Cover up a nail with this. ~ ENAMEL
A63. The man who said he understood the Einstein Theory did this. ~ LIED
A64. To augur. ~ OMEN
A67. Lots of sleepers pass through this state in the daytime ~ COMA
A68. Spoken. ~ ORAL
A69. The fifth at a bridge game. ~ BORE
A70. The land of traffic cops. ~ ERIN
A71. A revolution in England. ~ GYRE
A72. A mess the army always gets into. ~ STEW
A73. Withered. ~ SERE

D1. A fashionable whip. ~ CROP
D2. This ran through the streets of Pompeii. ~ LAVA
D3. To prove a plea. ~ AVER
D4. This chap is always down in the mouth. ~ DENTIST
D5. A black drawing-room suite. ~ SPADE
D6. To do a knotty piece of work. ~ TAT
D7. Gone by. ~ AGO
D8. What Peggy Joyce's husbands say it with. ~ GEMS
D9. What the girl who went on a diet did. ~ CRAVED
D10. Enthusiasm for sunburned shades of stockings. ~ RAGE
D11. A genus of trees. ~ ACER
D12. The kind of twins storks never bring. ~ BEDS
D20. You must do this if you expect your horse to win the race. ~ ENTER
D22. The morning after. ~ AM
D24. A little papa. ~ PA
D25. This is given away free on Wall Street. ~ TIP
D27. Squeal (Slang). ~ BLAB
D28. Hand this to your girl friend on her birthday. ~ LINE
D29. A prerequisite to drawing. ~ ANTE
D31. A good trap player. ~ RAT
D33. Transported. ~ RAPT
D34. The best way to turn fried eggs. ~ OVER
D35. So's your old Frenchman. ~ PERE
D37. This is used for sipping sodas. ~ LIP
D39. When they greet you this should be given a squeeze. ~ LEMON
D43. The chap who picks-up around the docks. ~ GOB
D45. Threats. ~ MENACES
D47. This will keep you guessing. ~ RIDDLE
D49. The baby says: "Very much obliged." ~ TA
D52. Toward. ~ TO
D54. What Scotchmen do with their worn-out clothes. ~ RENEW
D55. Tooth-paste caps will do this to your washstand. ~ CLOG
D56. Delicate. ~ AIRY
D57. United States beer. ~ NEAR
D58. What the night club does to pay its overhead. ~ ROBS
D60. What good stuff feels like. ~ MORE
D61. An official who drinks Turkish coffee. ~ EMIR
D62. This is long and has no turning. ~ LANE
D65. A wise-crack. ~ MOT
D66. Before. ~ ERE


